    "body": "> Also, that would mean that you'd have to load all the data into the DOM for find in page to work. For example, imagine the github code viewer. They'd have to load and render the DOM for the entire source file to get all the matches. That would be untenable for particularly large files.\r\n\r\nMy intent was that you'd load enough data for the next match, and perhaps even automatically scroll to it. Then, when you get a \"findinginpagenext\" or \"findinginpageprevious\" event, you'd load enough data to make _that_ available. Etc.",
