    "created_at": "2018-01-30T03:18:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-30T03:18:16Z",
    "body": "One thing I'm noting so far is that almost all web apps seem to just want to hijack the default search. GitHub wants to add regexp matching since it's targeted at developers. Discourse gives a very different search results display in its search box, with the option of expanding its search beyond just the current topic. Docs and Sheets have no extra features, but hijack it anyway; maybe they are our best use cases for people who would want the browser's built-in UI?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
